":"[3,3,3,4]","g":1},{"in":["[[34489505,617701],[34489506,36656],[34489505,184607],[34489503,787989],[34489507,394317],[34489504,1],[34489502,625876],[34489503,678360]]"],"out":"[617701,654357,838964,1626953,2021270,2021270,2647146,3325506]","g":1},{"in":["[[61337382,2],[87956169,5],[87956169,5],[87956169,5],[87956169,2],[61337382,2],[87956169,5],[61337382,5],[61337382,5],[87956169,5]]"],"out":"[2,5,10,15,17,17,22,22,22,27]","g":1},{"in":["[[29824710,1]]"],"out":"[1]","g":1},{"in":["[[16,778327],[7,275990],[5,284760],[15,751660],[4,836555],[17,768703],[4,3214],[4,954239],[16,759037]]"],"out":"[778327,1054317,1339077,2090737,2927292,3695995,3699209,4653448,5412485]","g":1},{"in":["[[20,456578],[14,456576],[13,456576],[10,456575],[11,456575],[1,456574],[17,456575]]"],"out":"[456578,913154,1369730,1826305,2282880,2739454,3196029]","g":1},{"in":["[[12,1000000],[14,1000000],[13,1000000],[13,1000000],[13,1000000]]"],"out":"[1000000,2000000,3000000,4000000,5000000]","g":1},{"in":["[[7,5],[13,5],[11,5],[8,4],[10,1],[8,4],[8,1],[12,2],[9,2],[12,4],[10,1]]"],"out":"[5,5,10,14,15,19,20,20,21,21,22]","g":1},{"in":["[[100000000,1],[88855193,1],[46474805,5],[69251405,1],[46465440,5],[36592132,1],[95543531,1],[18107755,5]]"],"out":"[1,1,5,5,5,5,5,5]","g":1},{"in":["[[90138732,2],[37582577,1],[61346587,2],[100000000,4],[82225989,3],[100000000,2],[21513606,5],[100000000,5]]"],"out":"[2,2,2,4,4,6,6,11]","g":1},{"in":["[[3,5]]"],"out":"[5]","g":1},{"in":["[[93202973,5],[93202967,5],[93202970,5]]"],"out":"[5,5,10]","g":1},{"in":["[[4,5],[20,5],[20,1],[4,1],[4,2],[20,3],[4,3],[4,4],[20,3],[20,2],[20,1],[4,5],[20,1]]"],"out":"[5,5,6,6,8,9,11,15,15,15,15,20,20]","g":1},{"in":["[[50466529,892259]]"],"out":"[892259]","g":1},{"in":["[[9,800465],[9,800462],[12,800463],[1,800464],[19,800462],[11,800464],[20,800464],[2,800465]]"],"out":"[800465,1600927,2401390,3201854,4002316,4802780,5603244,6403709]","g":1},{"in":["[[13,3],[12,3],[12,3]]"],"out":"[3,6,9]","g":1},{"in":["[[100000000,723670],[42435529,723670],[100000000,723670]]"],"out":"[723670,723670,1447340]","g":1},{"in":["[[7938437,1]]"],"out":"[1]","g":1},{"in":["[[6,5],[10,5],[15,1],[1,5],[20,5]]"],"out":"[5,10,10,10,10]","g":1},{"in":["[[44012353,1000000],[5978431,625926]]"],"out":"[1000000,1000000]","g":1},{"in":["[[15027329,944091],[35988827,944097],[100000000,944091],[68055742,944097],[93430794,944092],[92803980,944096],[38699301,944097],[67449214,944091],[68023301,944091],[19964520,944092]]"],"out":"[944091,944097,944097,944097,944097,1888188,1888188,1888188,2832279,2832279]","g":1},{"in":["[[36225214,172914],[63868748,947280],[98726835,1000000],[38142766,580838],[56494845,772966],[87926367,1000000],[1,1000000],[1,1],[99480164,1],[71164057,1]]"],"out":"[172914,947280,1000000,1000000,1000000,1000000,1000000,1000001,1000001,1000001]","g":1},{"in":["[[84865964,5],[98242951,4],[100000000,5],[1,3],[81476213,4],[45214708,3],[1,5]]"],"out":"[5,5,5,5,5,5,8]","g":1},{"in":["[[9,755157],[9,755157],[1,755157],[17,755157],[1,755157],[18,755157],[4,755157],[7,755157],[10,574950]]"],"out":"[755157,1510314,2265471,3020628,3775785,4530942,5286099,6041256,6616206]","g":1},{"in":["[[61778574,3],[61778572,5],[61778569,5],[61778569,2],[61778575,2]]"],"out":"[3,8,13,15,15]","g":1},{"in":["[[79464926,4]]"],"out":"[4]","g":1}],"lesson":"range-queries","statement":"Squares are dropped one at a time onto the x-axis. Each `positions[i] = [left, side]` is a square with side length `side` whose left edge is at `left`. It falls straight down until it lands on the x-axis or on top of an earlier square, and then stays there. Squares that only touch at an edge do not support each other.\n\nAfter each square lands, record the height of the tallest stack so far. Return those heights.","constraints":["1 <= positions.length <= 1000","Each square is [left, side] with 1 ≤ left ≤ 10⁸ and 1 ≤ side ≤ 10⁶"],"hints":["A square covers the half-open interval [left, left + side). It lands on the highest existing square that overlaps that interval.","With at most 1000 squares, an O(n²) solution is fine: for each new square, check every earlier square for overlap and take the maximum height.","Its new height is that maximum + side. Keep a running maximum for the answer. A segment tree with coordinate compression is the scalable version."],"explain":"The first square lands at height 2. The second overlaps it and lands on top, reaching 2 + 3 = 5. The third falls on empty ground at height 1, so the tallest stack stays 5: `[2,5,5]`."}
